Keep a shared numbers as an empty list of whole numbers.
Place 9 into numbers.
Place 1 into numbers.
Place 2 into numbers.
Place 3 into numbers.
Place 9 into numbers.
Keep a shared count as 0.
Keep a shared groups as 0.
Set count to 5.
Set groups to 3.
Keep a shared prefix as an empty list of whole numbers.
Place 0 into prefix.
For every spot from 0 to count minus 1.
The running is item spot of prefix plus item spot of numbers.
Place running into prefix.

Keep a shared table as an empty list of decimals.
The size is (groups plus 1) times (count plus 1).
For every spot from 0 to size minus 1.
Place 0.0 into table.

Keep a shared choice as a decimal.
To search from start (a whole number) with group (a whole number).
Set choice to -1.0.
For every cut from start plus 1 to count minus group plus 1.
The leftsum is item cut of prefix minus item start of prefix.
The span is (cut minus start) as a decimal.
The leftavg is leftsum as a decimal divided by span.
The right is item ((group minus 1) times (count plus 1) plus cut) of table.
The candidate is leftavg plus right.
If candidate is more than choice, set choice to candidate.

For every start from 0 to count minus 1.
The end is count.
The total is item end of prefix minus item start of prefix.
The leftlength is (count minus start) as a decimal.
The average is total as a decimal divided by leftlength.
Set item ((count plus 1) plus start) of table to average.

For every group from 2 to groups.
For every start from 0 to count minus group.
Search from start with group.
Set item (group times (count plus 1) plus start) of table to choice.

The answer is item (groups times (count plus 1)) of table.
Report answer.
